    "body": "<div>\n            \n  <div class=\"section\">\n\n<p>Emergency password reset when you can’t get into the admin interface.</p>\n<div class=\"section\">\n<h2>Why</h2>\n<p>Sometimes it happens that you want to reset an user’s password from\nthe Erlang shell.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"section\">\n<h2>Assumptions</h2>\n<p>Readers are expected to be familiar with the EShell for running Erlang code interactively.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"section\">\n<h2>How</h2>\n<p>You can do this from the Erlang shell without using the /admin or the reset-password mail/dialog.</p>\n<p>First go to the Erlang shell:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight-erlang notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"n\">marc</span><span class=\"sc\">$ </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">bin</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">zotonic</span> <span class=\"n\">shell</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<p>And then from the Erlang command prompt:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight-erlang notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">zotonic</span><span class=\"p\">@</span><span class=\"n\">host</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"nn\">m_identity</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nf\">set_username_pw</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1234</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s\">&quot;username&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s\">&quot;password&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nn\">z_acl</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nf\">sudo</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nn\">z</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">yoursitename</span><span class=\"p\">))).</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<p>Where <cite>1234</cite> is the id of your user (this must be an integer), <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">yoursitename</span></code> is the name of your site.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"section\">\n<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>\n<p>If you get the error:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight-erlang notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">admin_password_cannot_be_set</span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<p>That means you are trying to change the password for the admin (user\n1). The admin password is not set in the database: you need to define\nyour admin password in the site’s config file, use the property\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">admin_password</span></code>. For more info on this, see\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"/id/doc_developerguide_sites#guide-site-anatomy\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">Anatomy of a site</span></a>.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n           </div>",
